  "label": "Democratic Norms and Electoral Legitimacy",
  "description": "The meme implicitly references the foundational principles of democratic governance, including the legitimacy of elections and the rule of law. The satirical suggestion that one 'can't lose' if there is no election is a commentary on the potential undermining of these norms, which are essential to the functioning of a democratic society.",
